ted values, not recomputed here. That removes our normalization from the picture and also means we cannot audit it.", "Cross-sectional exposure: markers and methylation are measured once, at baseline. Only the outcome is longitudinal."], "survey": {"weighted": true, "weight": "survey_weight", "variance": "design", "n_strata": 28, "n_psu": 57, "lonely_psu_strata": 0, "population_size": 75754006, "population_deaths": 35727943, "nested_test": "design_wald"}}